1790415354 The ratio is on the query time row, which is what each engine says the
1790415354 queries cost it and what the public board publishes. The wall clock row
1790415354 above it also holds a process start per query, which is this harness and
1790415354 not the engine, and on a small sample it is most of what separates them.
1790415354 
1790415354 These ran every query at about the same speed:
1790415354   duckdb ran every query within 2.00x of every other one, and this suite spreads over 6x on an engine it is measuring
1790415354 A column that flat is not a column about the queries. Whatever every query
1790415354 in it has in common is larger than the difference between a count and a
1790415354 self join, and in this harness the thing they have in common is the process
1790415354 that gets started to ask. Read those numbers as an upper bound on the
1790415354 engine and not as a measurement of it.
1790415354 
1790415354 Hot here means the tries after the first, with every cache as the first
1790415354 try left it. Servers were restarted before each query's first try, so
1790415354 nothing carries from one query to the next.
